<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NB - no buyer T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	    PREV</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> 15 Mar-15 Apr    4/7 P	 16 Mar-15 Apr   5/7 P</p>
<p> April	   5 D/even	 April	   1 D/2 P</p>
<p> May		  8/3 D	 May		 7/1 D</p>
<p> July		 2/7 P	 July	     6/10 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> March	  1.5/0.5 D	 March	2 D/even</p>
<p> May		15/14 D	 May	 19 D/ n/a</p>
<p> July	   19.5/15 D	 July	  16/10 D</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> March	    85/70 D	 March	100/80 D</p>
<p> May	    110/100 D	 May	  130/90 D</p>
<p> July	   150/110 D	 July	160/120 D</p>
<p> August	 150/110 D	 August    130/110 D</p>
